            {
              "at": 1794318665283,
              "id": "6f7ab11f:answer",
              "kind": "text",
              "done": true,
              "text": "## What this project does\n\n**harbor** is a small static site generator. It turns Markdown pages into HTML using Go templates.\n\n| Folder | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `content/` | Markdown pages and their front matter |\n| `templates/` | Go templates used to render pages |\n| `public/` | Generated output, replaced by each build |\n\n## Main entry point\n\n`main.go` contains `main()`. It dispatches the `build` command to `Site.Build()` in `build.go`, or the `serve` command to a local preview of the generated output.\n\nStart with `main.go` for command handling and `build.go` for page rendering.\n\n## Tests\n\n`build_test.go` contains `TestBuildRendersPages`. It creates a temporary page and template, builds the site, and checks the generated HTML.\n\nThe test command, from the repository root, is:\n\n```sh\ngo test ./...\n```\n\nI only read the files. **No tests were run, no dependencies were installed, and no files were changed.**",
              "seq": 4
            },
